// FindingWhereGoneGone Always `true`. What the finding sat on was deleted.
type FindingWhereGoneGone bool

// FindingWhereGoneKind defines model for FindingWhereGone.Kind.
type FindingWhereGoneKind string

// FindingWhereOrGone What a finding sits on, as an answer gives it: the entry, or that the entry is gone. Only an
// answer carries the second; a finding is never raised on something gone.
type FindingWhereOrGone struct {
	union json.RawMessage
}

// FindingWhereValue What it sits on, or that it was deleted since: the finding stays when it is
// (ONPLO-2427). `null` only for a finding whose Against names a framework requirement,
// which may sit on nothing (the Where field: "Required unless Against names a framework
// requirement").
type FindingWhereValue = FindingWhereOrGone

// Framework ONE FRAMEWORK IN SCOPE — a lens over the one control library, and never a library of its
// own. Not on it yet: its version and jurisdiction (ONPLO-1950). Its requirements are
// `listFrameworkRequirements`, and its readiness is never on it: that is counted when asked,
// and is `FrameworkReadiness`. (This said who answers for it waited on ONPLO-1629, point 4,
