// ScoredRiskRating A rating as a risk answers it: the two picks, and the score and band worked out from them on
// the scale in force. A score and a band are never sent: what is kept is the picks.
type ScoredRiskRating struct {
	// Band "Three bands, cut at thirds of the highest score": `low` up to a third of it, `medium` up to
	// two thirds, `high` above, each cut rounded down — 3 and 6 on a 3×3 scale, 8 and 16 on a 5×5.
	// What the heat view colours by, so the same band is the same share of the scale whatever its
	// size.
	Band RiskBand `json:"band"`

	// Impact One pick on one axis, counted from 1 — the lowest level. The scale is 3×3 unless somebody
	// chose 5×5, so a pick is never above 5, and above 3 only where the scale is 5×5.
	Impact RiskPick `json:"impact"`

	// Likelihood One pick on one axis, counted from 1 — the lowest level. The scale is 3×3 unless somebody
	// chose 5×5, so a pick is never above 5, and above 3 only where the scale is 5×5.
	Likelihood RiskPick `json:"likelihood"`

	// Score "A score is likelihood × impact": the two picks multiplied, so 1 to 9 on a 3×3 scale and 1 to
	// 25 on a 5×5. Worked out on the scale in force each time the risk is read, and never kept.
	Score RiskScore `json:"score"`
}

// SettableControlStatus THE THREE WORDS A PERSON MAY SET (decision 0652). `ControlStatus` without `failing`, which
// is never set by hand. A list of its own rather than a sentence beside the other one, so
// that a request carrying `failing` is refused by the shape and no handler has to remember.
type SettableControlStatus string

// SettableFindingState THE THREE STATES `updateFinding` TAKES. `FindingState` without `fixed` and
// `accepted-risk`, each of which waits on a page (ONPLO-1969, point 1; ONPLO-1864). A list
// of its own, so that a request carrying either is refused by the shape.
type SettableFindingState string

// Steward WHO ANSWERS FOR A CONTROL, day to day. The control belongs to the account environment; the
// steward is the one who is asked, the page's word and the glossary's (until 22 October 2026
// the page said owner, ONPLO-1016 point 4). A FINDING NAMES ONE THE SAME WAY: its page says "a steward,
// the same word and the same check against identity as a control's". A framework and a policy
// are answered for by a person alone, and name one with `PersonSteward`.
//
// A PERSON OR A TEAM (ONPLO-3314). The control's configuration block says "The person or the
// team that answers for the control day to day". A team is asked about of identity as a
// scope's team is, and one that is not a team of this account environment is refused under
// the same `steward_not_found` as a person who is not here. (A person alone until 26 October
// 2026, while nothing answered this service whether a team is here, ONPLO-2182. This said
// the block named "the person accountable" until 22 October 2026, ONPLO-1016 point 4.)
//
// A TEAM'S MEMBERS DO NOT GET ITS TASKS YET. "A team answers as a team: each of its members
// gets the control's tasks." A finding answered for by a team raises its overdue task to
// nobody yet, so it waits in the task list until somebody picks it up, as a row with no
// steward does (ONPLO-3380).
type Steward struct {
	// Id A person's id, minted by Account, or a team's, minted by identity, as `kind` says.
	// Compliance holds the id and re-enters nothing else about either: the roster is
	// Account's, and the team is identity's.
	Id   Id          `json:"id"`
	Kind StewardKind `json:"kind"`
}

// StewardKind defines model for Steward.Kind.
type StewardKind string

// ThresholdDays A number of days. At least one; at most ten years, a bound of this API and not of any page.
type ThresholdDays = int

// TimeZoneName An IANA zone name, `Europe/Brussels` — the zone a person chose a moment in, so a screen
// shows it back in that zone and "until 17:00 Brussels" never returns as another hour.
//
// THE PATTERN REFUSES NONSENSE, AND THE SERVICE REFUSES THE REST, as Account's preferences
// do (`Preferences.time_zone`). The real list moves several times a year and lives in the
// runtime's own zone database, not in a contract, so `Mars/Olympus` passes this pattern; the
// service asks that database, and answers a zone no clock knows, or a bare offset such as
// `+01`, with a 422 naming the field.
//
// Examples: Europe/Brussels
type TimeZoneName = string

// Timestamp RFC 3339, always UTC, always with the offset written out.
//
// Examples: 2026-09-13T06:06:00Z
type Timestamp = time.Time

// TrustCenter WHAT ONE ACCOUNT ENVIRONMENT'S TRUST CENTER SHOWS, AND WHETHER IT IS PUBLISHED. Every field
// is always present.
//
// IT IS PUBLISHED EXACTLY WHILE `published_at` IS A MOMENT AND `taken_down_at` IS `null`.
// There is no state field to disagree with that. Never published: both `null`. Taken down:
// both moments, `taken_down_at` the later.
type TrustCenter struct {
	// Access Who may open a document. It starts `public`, the page's default.
	Access TrustCenterAccessValue `json:"access"`

	// Address Where a stranger opens the published page; `null` until it is first published, and
	// kept for ever after, taken down or not.
	Address *TrustCenterAddressValue `json:"address"`

	// NotifyMeOfChanges WHETHER THE PUBLIC PAGE OFFERS "NOTIFY ME OF CHANGES" — "a subscribe box on the public
	// page (email only, one-click unsubscribe, no Onplo account)". It starts `true`. Turning
	// it off removes nobody already subscribed.
	NotifyMeOfChanges bool `json:"notify_me_of_changes"`

	// PublishedAt When it was last published; `null` while it never was.
	PublishedAt *Timestamp `json:"published_at"`

	// Sections The sections shown, in the order this list declares them, each once. It starts at
	// "certs + sub-processors"; none at all is a page that shows nothing but its name.
	Sections []TrustCenterSection `json:"sections"`

	// TakenDownAt When it was taken down; `null` while it is published or never was.
	TakenDownAt *Timestamp `json:"taken_down_at"`
}

// TrustCenterAccess WHO MAY OPEN A DOCUMENT — "Fully public, or gated behind a request/NDA click for sensitive
// documents". The page's default for its documents, `public` until it is changed; a rule per
// document arrives with the documents themselves (ONPLO-3190, change 4).
type TrustCenterAccess string

// TrustCenterAccessValue Who may open a document. It starts `public`, the page's default.
