	//
	// "THE RECIPIENTS ARE CONFIRMED BEFORE THE NOTICE IS SIGNED OFF." Everyone it proposes now is
	// confirmed, and the answer is the notice. Somebody who subscribes later is proposed and not
	// confirmed, so is told only once this is called again. A subscriber removed from the Trust
	// Center is "sent nothing further", and is gone from here too.
	//
	// CONFIRMING NOBODY NEW CHANGES NOTHING. Confirming somebody new changes who the notice goes to,
	// so it is a change like any other: its `version` moves on, and "changing a signed-off notice
	// takes the sign-off away".
	//
	// REFUSED, AND WRITES NOTHING. Nobody proposed is `no_recipients`, which is what a notice to the
	// affected people answers until a file adds its addresses (`addIncidentNoticeAddressFile`). A CLOSED INCIDENT IS READ AND
	// NOT WORKED, `incident_closed`.
