	// FileIncidentObligationStepWithBody Record a filing on one step of an incident's obligation
	//
	// "Onplo assembles the notification an authority asks for and you file it in your own
	// authority's portal — no supervisory authority accepts a filing from a third-party system.
	// Record here when it was submitted, by whom, and the authority's reference; attach the
	// receipt. The RECORD is the evidence." Recording one is a permission of its own (ONPLO-2336).
	//
	// WHAT IT MOVES. A step that counts from this one gets its due moment, counted from the moment
	// this one was filed. An obligation whose every step is filed is Met, and an incident whose
	// obligations are all Met or Dismissed may be closed. The answer is the obligation as it now
	// stands.
	//
	// A STEP IS FILED ONCE, `step_filed`: the record is the evidence, and evidence is not written
	// over. A STEP THAT COUNTS FROM AN EARLIER ONE waits for that one, `earlier_step_unfiled`,
	// since it has no clock until then. A DISMISSED OBLIGATION IS NOT FILED, `obligation_dismissed`:
	// it was said not to be owed. A CLOSED INCIDENT IS READ AND NOT WORKED, `incident_closed`.
	//
	// WHO FILED IT is a member of this environment, named in the request, because the person who
	// submitted it in the authority's portal is not always the one recording it here. WHO RECORDED
	// IT AND WHEN are written from the call's own credential and the moment it arrives.
	//
	// THE RECEIPT IS A FILE ALREADY IN STORAGE, named by its id, as evidence is: what is kept is
	// the file's id and the save Storage calls current at this moment, never sent by the caller.
	// A file you may not see is `file_not_found`.
	//
	// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
	//
	// Corresponds with POST /incidents/{incident_id}/obligations/{obligation_id}/steps/{step}/filing (the `FileIncidentObligationStep` operationId).
