// CreateAssessmentWithBody Start an assessment from the thing it judges
//
// "AN ASSESSMENT IS NEVER FREE-FLOATING: IT IS CREATED FROM THE THING IT JUDGES — a processing
// activity on Systems & data, a vendor (a supplier), or an AI system." A processing activity
// is an entry of the asset and data register. It starts as a draft with every answer empty.
//
// THE TEMPLATE FOLLOWS FROM WHAT IT JUDGES WHEN IT IS LEFT OUT: the AI system template for an
// AI system record, the data protection template for a register entry or a vendor. The AI
// system template is for an AI system record alone, because it sits beside "the risk tier
// recorded on the system"; asked of anything else it is refused 422 at `/template`. An AI
// system that handles personal data takes both, one at a time.
//
// A THING HAS AT MOST ONE ASSESSMENT PER TEMPLATE. A second is refused `assessment_exists`
// and nothing is written; the one it has is revised, never replaced.
//
// THE STEWARD STARTS AS THE MEMBER WHO OPENED IT when none is named. A steward that is named
// is asked about, as `createControl` asks (decision 0670).
//
// A RETIRED VENDOR OR A RETIRED AI SYSTEM RECORD IS NOT REFUSED. No page says an assessment
// may not be started for one, and an auditor asking about last year may need it.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
//
