// PlaceConfidentialHoldWithBody Place a Confidential legal hold
//
// THE SECOND MODE, AND THE ONLY ONE THAT HIDES ANYTHING (decision 0455). It is a legal hold
// in every way `placeLegalHold` describes — it freezes, it refuses no delete, it is in force
// when this answers — and it is HIDDEN FROM THE PEOPLE IT NAMES: for them there is no badge,
// no ghost and no notice on release. "Everyone else's view is unchanged."
//
// IT SAYS WHO IT IS HIDDEN FROM, AND IT CANNOT BE PLACED WITHOUT (decision 0687). "The one or
// more PEOPLE the hold is hidden from, named by whoever places it, whatever is held … A hold
// on a folder says who; nothing is worked out from who owns the folder or who can open it. A
// person not named sees the hold like everyone else." A hold on a person names that person
// here like anybody else: nothing is filled in.
//
// WHOEVER PLACES IT IS NEVER ON IT. "Placing or adding refuses the caller's own name, pointing
// at this field, because nobody investigates themself and a hold its placer cannot see is one
// mistake away from a hold nobody releases." It is the 422 at `hidden_from`
// (`hidden_from_names_the_placer`), and nothing is asked or placed.
//
// EACH PERSON NAMED IS SOMEBODY IN THIS ACCOUNT ENVIRONMENT, asked of the identity service
// before anything is placed, as a control's steward is (decision 0670). Anybody else is
// refused `hidden_from_not_found`, and the answer never says which name or why. When
// identity cannot be asked the answer is `identity_unavailable` and no hold is in force.
//
// IT HIDES THE FACT OF THE HOLD, NEVER A PERSON'S OWN THINGS. "Even a Confidential hold hides
// only the fact of the hold, never a person's own files."
//
// THE ANSWER IS THE HOLD AS ANY HOLD READS, without the list. Whom it is hidden from is
// answered by `listHoldHiddenFrom`, on a permission of its own.
//
// ITS OWN PERMISSION, AND THE HIGHER ONE: "it requires the higher Compliance role plus a
// written reason and authority". Ring 1, a named person, never a raw key and never an agent.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
//
// Corresponds with POST /confidential-holds (the `PlaceConfidentialHold` operationId).
