// CreateControlWithBody Write a control
//
// A CONTROL IS A PLAIN STATEMENT AND SOMEBODY WHO ANSWERS FOR IT — "Production access is
// reviewed quarterly", and a named person. Both are required on the screen and both are
// required here: every control has a steward, and a control nobody answers for is the thing
// an auditor finds first.
//
// THE STEWARD IS SAID, NEVER DEFAULTED. In a personal account environment you are every
// steward, and a client sends your own id; the API does not assume it for you, because a
// company's control must never be made yours by a field left out.
//
// THE STEWARD IS SOMEBODY IN THIS ACCOUNT ENVIRONMENT, AND THAT IS ASKED ON EVERY WRITE THAT
// NAMES ONE (decision 0670). A person who is a member here today may be named, a suspended
// member included: "a suspension is not a departure". Anybody else is refused
