// THE STATUS IS NOT HERE. A status has a rule of its own — a control is "never marked
// satisfied without evidence" — and a rule of its own gets an operation of its own
// (decision 0547), never a field in a patch body. That operation is `setControlStatus`.
//
// A STEWARD IS REPLACED, NEVER REMOVED. Every control has one, so there is no way to clear
// the field.
//
// A STEWARD THAT IS NAMED IS ASKED ABOUT, as `createControl` asks (decision 0670) — the one the
// control already has included, so a change that names somebody who has left is refused
// `steward_not_found` whoever they are. A change that names no steward asks nothing. When the
// identity service cannot be asked, the answer is `identity_unavailable` and nothing changed.
//
// A RETIRED CONTROL IS NOT CHANGED: `control_retired`, and nothing is written
// (`retireControl`). It is asked once the control is read, so a change that names a steward
// who has left is refused about the steward first.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
//
// Corresponds with PATCH /controls/{control_id} (the `UpdateControl` operationId).
