// AttachEvidenceWithBody Attach a file to a control as evidence
//
// PUT THE PROOF WHERE THE CLAIM IS. A file, a screenshot, an export — attached to the control
// it proves, time-stamped and with the name of whoever attached it.
//
// THE FILE IS ALREADY IN STORAGE, AND IT IS NAMED BY ITS ID. This operation uploads nothing
// and copies nothing: the bytes count once, where they live, and what is kept here is the id.
// A reference between two apps is an id — never a path, never a copy. A file that is not in
// Storage yet is uploaded by `startEvidenceUpload`.
//
// A FILE YOU MAY NOT SEE IS REFUSED AS IF IT DID NOT EXIST — `file_not_found`. Saying which
// would tell somebody a file exists in a folder they cannot open. A folder is refused the
// same way: evidence is a file.
//
// THE VERSION IS RECORDED. A file's id survives every save, so the answer carries which
// version of the file was current at the moment it was attached. Whether a reader is later
// shown that version or the file as it stands is not on any page (ONPLO-1016, point 11);
// the fact is kept so that either answer stays possible.
//
// STORAGE IS ASKED WHICH SAVE IS CURRENT, AS YOU, and a file it cannot answer about is
// `file_not_found`. Storage that could not be asked is the 503 `storage_unavailable`, and
// nothing is attached: a file nobody could check is never recorded. No such control is
// refused first, and Storage is not asked about a file for it.
//
// IT MOVES NO STATUS. Proof makes Implemented possible and sets nothing; the control's
// history records the item, by its id, in the audit event this leaves.
//
// A RETIRED CONTROL TAKES NO NEW EVIDENCE: `control_retired`, asked before Storage is, and
// nothing is attached (`retireControl`). What it already has stays.
//
// UNDER A MANUAL SOURCE, OR STRAIGHT ON THE CONTROL. The page: a file attached by hand "is
// attached either under a manual source, and then proves that source's controls, or straight
// onto one or several controls with no source; its item then reads 'By hand'". Naming
// `evidence_source_id` attaches it under that source: the item proves every control the source
// names at that moment that is in use, the one in the address among them, and is read under
// each. A retired control among them takes nothing, as above. Left out, the item names no
// source and its `evidence_source_id` is `null`: it proves the control in the address and each
// one `other_control_ids` names. A body naming both is the 422.
//
// A CONTROL YOU NAME IS REFUSED, NEVER PASSED OVER, AND BEFORE STORAGE IS ASKED. In
// `other_control_ids`, one that is not here is `control_not_found` and one retired is
// `control_retired`, and either way nothing is attached.
//
// THE SOURCE IS ASKED ABOUT BEFORE STORAGE IS. One you may not see, or none, is
// `evidence_source_not_found`. One that is not manual is `evidence_source_not_manual`: an
// automated source or one from Onplo collects its own proof, and nothing is attached under it
// by hand. One that does not name the control in the address is
// `evidence_source_not_on_control`. Each way nothing is attached.
//
// ONE AUDIT EVENT PER CONTROL IT PROVES, each in that control's history, naming the item.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
//
// Corresponds with POST /controls/{control_id}/evidence-items (the `AttachEvidence` operationId).
func (c *Client) AttachEvidenceWithBody(ctx context.Context, controlId ControlId, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*http.Response, error) {
	req, err := NewAttachEvidenceRequestWithBody(c.Server, controlId, contentType, body)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	req = req.WithContext(ctx)
	if err := c.applyEditors(ctx, req, reqEditors); err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return c.Client.Do(req)
}

