// LinkControlToRequirement Say a control answers a framework requirement
//
// "WHICH FRAMEWORK REQUIREMENTS A CONTROL SATISFIES" is in the control's configuration. A
// control picked from one of Onplo's ready-made controls is already linked to what Onplo
// maps that one to; a control a person wrote is linked to nothing until somebody links it
// here. From then on readiness counts it: the requirement is done when every control linked
// to it is Implemented.
//
// WHICH REQUIREMENT. One of a framework in scope in this account environment, by the id
// `listFrameworkRequirements` answers. Any other id is refused `requirement_not_found`. A
// control may answer requirements of several frameworks: "map once, prove many".
//
// A LINK THAT IS ALREADY THERE CHANGES NOTHING AND ANSWERS 204, so a retry whose answer was
// lost is not a second link. A person may also link a picked control, to a requirement
// Onplo does not map it to.
//
// AT MOST 100 CONTROLS A REQUIREMENT, counting Onplo's and a person's links together, so the
// requirement's row always lists all of them. A 101st is refused `requirement_controls_full`.
//
// A RETIRED CONTROL IS NOT LINKED: `control_retired`, a link already there included
// (`retireControl`). Its links stay as they were, and count toward nothing.
//
// AT MOST 100 COUNTS THE CONTROLS IN USE. A retired control linked to the requirement is not
// among the 100, as it is not among the controls the requirement's row lists.
