// A ROW IS WHAT IS WRONG, HOW BAD, WHO ANSWERS FOR FIXING IT, WHERE IT SITS, WHAT IT BREAKS,
// WHEN IT MUST BE FIXED BY AND WHERE IT STANDS. Not on it, each with what holds it: how it
// was raised, by hand or by which source, and the evidence of its fix (ONPLO-1969, points 6
// and 1); and its effectiveness re-check, whose "one cycle" has no length (point 4).
//
// NO FILTER YET. The page's saved Nonconformities filter is the findings whose Against names
// a framework requirement. One can be named since ONPLO-4571, and each such finding answers
// it in `against`; a list narrowed to them is not served yet. (This said no requirement could
// be named here until then, ONPLO-1629 point 6.)
