// UpdateIncidentWithBody Work an incident
//
// "WORK AN INCIDENT — SET ITS SEVERITY, LINK THE ASSETS AND CONTROLS IT TOUCHED, MARK IT
// CONTAINED AND WRITE IT UP." Every field optional; an omitted one is left as it is.
//
// CONTAINED IS THE ONE STATE SET HERE. "Contained once the cause is stopped." Closing and
// reopening are acts of their own, `closeIncident` and `reopenIncident`, and no page says an
// incident marked contained goes back to Open; nothing here moves it back.
//
// WHAT IT TOUCHED IS REGISTER ENTRIES AND CONTROLS OF THIS LIBRARY, by id. An id that names
// none is refused, `register_entry_not_found` or `control_not_found`, and nothing changes.
//
// "PRODUCT AFFECTED (CRA)" is set here, with the moment kept (`product_affected_since`). Set to
// an exploited vulnerability or a severe incident while the CRA is in scope, it owes the CRA's
// report from that moment, as working the incident owes any other; the event names each
// obligation it added. A FIX OR MITIGATION BEING AVAILABLE is recorded here too, with its zone,
// and only on an exploited vulnerability: on any other is `422` at `/body/fix_available_at`, and
// so is a moment ahead of now or one sent without its zone; a zone no clock knows is `422` at
// `/body/fix_available_at_zone`. Set to anything but an exploited vulnerability, the recorded
// moment goes with it.
//
// "AI SYSTEM INVOLVED" AND "SERIOUS INCIDENT (EU AI ACT)" are set here: the AI systems of the
// register it involves, by id, the whole list each time, and which serious incident it is, or
// `null`. An id that names no AI system of this account environment is refused,
// `ai_system_record_not_found`, and nothing changes. With the EU AI Act in scope, a system of
// tier `high` named and a case said, it owes the EU AI Act's report, as working the incident
// owes any other. A widespread infringement is ticked beside a case, never alone.
//
// A CLOSED INCIDENT IS READ AND NOT WORKED, and is refused with `incident_closed`: reopening
// it comes first.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
//
// Corresponds with PATCH /incidents/{incident_id} (the `UpdateIncident` operationId).
