// "YOUR CUSTOMERS: ONE STEP, WITHIN 48 HOURS. CONTRACTS DIFFER, SO THE STEWARD MAY CHANGE
// THAT MOMENT ON THIS INCIDENT, WITH THE REASON KEPT" (ONPLO-2336). The moment sent becomes
// the due moment of the obligation's one step, its `due_set_by` is `steward`, and the move
// joins its `due_moves`: the moment before, the moment after, the reason, who moved it and
// when. Nothing else of it moves. The answer is the obligation as it now stands.
//
// ONLY YOUR CUSTOMERS' ONE, AND ONLY BY ITS STEWARD. Every other step's moment is the law's,
// or Onplo's reminder the page names as Onplo's, and is refused `due_not_movable`. A caller
// who is not the obligation's steward now is refused `not_steward`, since the page gives the
// moment to the steward; an agent is never a steward, so an agent is always refused.
//
// WHAT IS REFUSED, AND WRITES NOTHING. Moving it to the moment it already has is
// `due_unchanged`. An obligation answers at most one hundred moves, and the one after is
// `due_moves_full`. A step already filed is `step_filed`, and a Dismissed obligation is
// `obligation_dismissed`: neither has a clock left to move. A CLOSED INCIDENT IS READ AND NOT
// WORKED, `incident_closed`. A moment before the obligation was first owed is refused under
// `/body/due_at`, since its clock had not started.
//
// WHO MOVED IT AND WHEN are written from the call's own credential and the moment it arrives.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
//
// Corresponds with POST /incidents/{incident_id}/obligations/{obligation_id}/due-move (the `MoveIncidentObligationDue` operationId).
