// ListLegalHolds The legal holds
//
// "LEGAL HOLDS LISTS EVERY HOLD IN FORCE AND EVERY RELEASED ONE." One row per hold, each the
// whole legal record as `LegalHold` describes it: a released hold stays on the list as a
// released hold, because "the record does not go".
//
// A HOLD THAT WAS NEVER IN FORCE IS NOT ON IT. A placement the deletion service could not be
// told of answered `freeze_unavailable`, and what it left behind is no hold.
//
// "A HOLD HIDDEN FROM YOU IS NOT IN YOUR LIST." A Confidential hold is absent for the people
// it is hidden from, with no gap and no count that says one was left out; for everyone else
// it is a row like any other, "with no sign it is Confidential" (decision 0687).
//
// OLDEST FIRST, by when each was placed, so a page already read does not move when a hold is
// placed.
//
// SEEING THE HOLDS IS A PERMISSION OF ITS OWN, and neither placing nor releasing carries it.
// Every look is recorded (decision 0675). (The top of this file listed "SEEING THE LEGAL
// HOLDS" as an absence until the catalogue gained the permission on 2026-10-09.)
//
// Corresponds with GET /legal-holds (the `ListLegalHolds` operationId).
