//
// "PLAN AN INTERNAL AUDIT ROUND OR START A MANAGEMENT REVIEW CYCLE'S PACK." `kind` says which.
// "You say which controls a round tests, who tests them, and how often the cycle comes round";
// a review names its period and who attends it.
//
// A ROUND'S CONTROLS ARE FIXED WHEN IT IS PLANNED. Left out, they are "the whole environment":
// every control in this library at that moment. A control written afterwards is in the next
// round, never this one, so that every item a verdict is recorded on was named when the round
// began. An id that names no control here is refused `control_not_found`. A round tests at
// most 2000 controls, a bound of this API that keeps the largest body under the request
// limit: a library larger than that names its controls, in more than one round, and leaving
// them out is refused 422 on `control_ids`.
//
// WHO PERFORMS IT IS A PERSON, CHECKED AGAINST IDENTITY as a control's steward is (decision
// 0670): the auditor of a round, the attendees of a review. Anybody who is not a member here
// today is refused `person_not_found`, and when identity cannot be asked the answer is
// `identity_unavailable`.
