// CreateRiskWithBody Register a risk
//
// A RISK IS A PLAIN SENTENCE AND TWO RATINGS — "The risk in plain language", and
// "Likelihood × Impact … taken twice: INHERENT (before controls) and RESIDUAL". All three
// are required, as they are on the screen.
//
// TYPED, OR KEPT FROM A SCENARIO. A risk can also be "accepted from the scenario library",
// which `listRiskScenarios` reads with each scenario's suggested rating on this environment's
// scale. "Keeping a scenario is one act: registering a risk. One write saves the risk with
// the suggested rating as adjusted and links the controls already picked." So a client
// copies the sentence into `name` and the suggestion, as adjusted, into the ratings, and
// names the scenario in `from_scenario_id`. The risk then records the scenario and the
// version it came from (`Risk.from_scenario`), and every control of this library picked from
// one of the scenario's ready-made controls is linked to it, beside any `linked_control_ids`
// sent. "A scenario you accept behaves exactly like a risk you typed yourself": the record
// changes nothing the risk does. The rest of the scenario's controls are then offered, and
// picking them is `pickReadyMadeControls` with this risk's id. It asks nothing more than
// registering a risk. (This said until 7 November 2026 that nothing recorded which scenario
// a risk came from, and that a client linked the controls by hand, ONPLO-3151. It said what a
// scenario suggests was on no page until ONPLO-2475 ruled it.)
//
// EACH PICK IS ON THIS ACCOUNT ENVIRONMENT'S SCALE. The scale is 3×3 unless somebody chose
// 5×5, and `getRiskScale` reads it. A pick above it is refused `rating_outside_scale`, and
// nothing is written. (This said seeing the scale "has no permission yet, so the refusal is
// how a caller learns it", and that nobody may see the scenario library, until decision 0804
// gave each a permission.)
//
// LINKED CONTROLS ARE CONTROLS IN THIS LIBRARY. An id that names none is refused
// `control_not_found`, and a scenario id that names none of Onplo's is refused
// `risk_scenario_not_found`; nothing is written either way. A risk is linked to at most 500
// controls, the ones sent and the scenario's together, and more is refused
// `risk_controls_full`.
//
// ITS TREATMENT IS MITIGATE UNLESS ANOTHER IS SENT — "Accept / Mitigate / Transfer / Avoid,
// with a note", default Mitigate. A risk registered with Accept is "Accept — awaiting
// sign-off" until somebody signs it (`signRiskAcceptance`): registering is not signing.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
//
// Corresponds with POST /risks (the `CreateRisk` operationId).
func (c *Client) CreateRiskWithBody(ctx context.Context, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*http.Response, error) {
	req, err := NewCreateRiskRequestWithBody(c.Server, contentType, body)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	req = req.WithContext(ctx)
	if err := c.applyEditors(ctx, req, reqEditors); err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return c.Client.Do(req)
}

