// UpdateRiskWithBody Re-assess a risk
//
// SCORE IT AGAIN, RE-LINK ITS CONTROLS, MOVE ITS REVIEW DATE, OR SAY IT BETTER. Every field
// optional, an omitted one untouched. `linked_control_ids` replaces the whole list: the list
// sent is the list kept.
//
// The same two refusals as `createRisk`, for the same reasons: `rating_outside_scale` and
// `control_not_found`. In both nothing changes.
//
// CHOOSING ITS TREATMENT — "choose its treatment with a note", part of this permission on
// the catalogue. `treatment` is the choice and its note together, and replaces both: a note
// left out is no note. A treatment of Accept is "Accept — awaiting sign-off" until somebody
// signs it (`signRiskAcceptance`), and choosing is never signing. ANY NEW CHOICE OR NOTE
// NEEDS SIGNING AGAIN: a signature is of the treatment it was given on, so changing the
// choice, or the note of a signed Accept, leaves the earlier signature on the record and
// the risk awaiting a new one. Sending the treatment the risk already has changes nothing.
// (This said choosing a treatment was not here, because accepting a risk had a signer on
// one page and none on another, until decision 0804 ruled ONPLO-1633, point 2.)
