// stopped using off this list … The record stays readable under Retired for the auditor"
// (decision 0779). So `retired=true` answers the retired vendors and nothing else, and
// without it a retired vendor is not listed. Never both in one list: the page shows two.
//
// A ROW IS A VENDOR'S NAME, WHETHER IT IS MARKED A SUB-PROCESSOR, WHEN IT WAS RETIRED, THE
// REGISTER ENTRIES IT TOUCHES AND ITS RISK TIER — suggested, set by hand, and the one in
// force (decision 0779, points 1 to 3; ONPLO-2250). (This said "the tier and the entries are
// declared in a change of their own" until 14 October 2026.) Not on it, each with what holds
// it:
//   - WHAT THE TIER'S RULES ASK FOR: the review date, the DPA and a published report. The rules
//     say what is required (`getVendorAssessmentRules`); nothing records yet whether a vendor
//     has it.
