	//
	// "SEE THE INCIDENT REGISTER." One register per account environment, every state in it, newest
	// first: a closed incident stays on the list and says so, because its write-up is evidence.
	//
	// A ROW IS WHAT HAPPENED, HOW BAD, WHERE IT STANDS, WHAT IT TOUCHED AND ITS WRITE-UP. Not on
	// it: its obligations with their clocks and the nearest deadline among them, seen under their
	// own permission (`listIncidentObligations`), and the notices to the affected people and
	// customers, read with `listIncidentNotices`.
