	// DraftIncidentNoticeWithBodyWithResponse Draft an incident's notice to one audience
	//
	// "DRAFTED BY THE APP, APPROVED BY YOU." A notice holds "what happened and when it was found,
	// which data and roughly how many people, the likely consequences, what was done to contain
	// it, what the reader should do now, and the contact point". Drafting one is working the
	// incident, so it is under that permission, which the catalogue lets an agent hold to draft:
	// the Compliance app's agent drafting a notice through this operation is the app drafting it.
	//
	// ONE NOTICE PER AUDIENCE IN THE MAKING. While an incident has a notice to that audience that
	// is not sent, another is refused, `notice_exists`, and that notice is changed instead
	// (`changeIncidentNotice`). "A sent notice is never changed: a correction is a new notice to the
	// same audience, and both are kept": once every notice to it is sent, a new one is drafted.
	// (Until 13 November 2026 a second was refused whether or not the first was sent; ONPLO-4974.)
	// A CLOSED INCIDENT IS READ AND NOT WORKED, `incident_closed`.
	//
	// WHO DRAFTED IT AND WHEN are written from the call's own credential and the moment it arrives.
	//
	// NOT HERE YET, each named so a reader knows it is missing and not forgotten (ONPLO-3923):
	//   * THE AFFECTED PEOPLE'S RECIPIENTS: the members and guests Account names, and a list of
	//     addresses from a Storage file (`listIncidentNoticeRecipients` says what is read today).
	//   * SENDING ONE, and recording the step of the obligation it meets. Until a notice can be
	//     sent, none is, so every notice can still be changed.
	//   * A CORRECTION. "A sent notice is never changed: a correction is a new notice to the same
	//     audience." It arrives with sending, and with it a second notice to one audience.
	//
	// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
	//
	// Corresponds with POST /incidents/{incident_id}/notices (the `DraftIncidentNotice` operationId).
