	// SendIncidentNoticeWithBodyWithResponse Send a signed-off notice
	//
	// "SEND AN APPROVED BREACH NOTICE TO THE AFFECTED PEOPLE AND TO CUSTOMERS." The version the
	// caller read, signed off, goes to everyone confirmed, one mail each, and the answer is the
	// notice, sent. Sending is its own act, beside signing it off.
	//
	// THE MAIL, as the Incidents page settles it (ONPLO-4974). From the company's name, "via Onplo".
	// Its subject is Onplo's own, "A security incident that may affect your data", and its body is
	// the notice's parts in the page's order, each under its heading, with nothing added. It goes
	// out in the notice's language: its words untranslated, and the subject and headings Onplo's
	// own in that language where Onplo has them and in English where it does not yet. It is a
	// notification to both audiences, so it carries no unsubscribe link.
