	// ListReadyMadeControlsWithResponse Onplo's ready-made controls
	//
	// WHAT ONPLO SHIPS, NEVER WHAT YOU HAVE. The ready-made controls Onplo writes and versions —
	// "content, not the company's own library". The list is the same in every account
	// environment, and reading it says nothing about anybody's controls. Your own library is
	// `listControls`, and it "starts empty": a control exists there only once somebody writes or
	// picks it (decision 0664).
	//
	// A ROW IS A STATEMENT AND A VERSION, "and nothing else yet". Which framework asks for a
	// ready-made control arrives with frameworks, and so does a filter by one.
	//
	// WHETHER ONE IS ALREADY IN YOUR LIBRARY IS NOT ON THE ROW. "One already picked shows as
	// picked", and what says so is the library: a picked control carries `picked_from`. This
	// list is gated by the permission to see what Onplo ships, and a row that answered it would
	// show part of the library on that permission.
	//
	// ITS OWN PERMISSION, beside seeing the library and beside picking: "seeing Onplo's
	// ready-made controls and picking one are each a permission of their own".
	//
	// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
	//
	// Corresponds with GET /ready-made-controls (the `ListReadyMadeControls` operationId).
