	//
	// "A VENDOR IS RETIRED, NEVER DELETED" (decision 0779). It leaves the list of vendors in
	// use, and "the record stays readable under Retired for the auditor": it opens by its id
	// and is listed with `retired=true`, each saying when it was retired.
	//
	// A POST AND NOT A DELETE, because the record does not go — as a released legal hold stays a
	// released hold. The permission is the catalogue's `.delete`: "Retire a vendor you stopped
	// using … Never undone."
