// ListAccessReviewCampaignsWithResponse The access-review campaigns scheduled here
//
// "SEE SCHEDULED CAMPAIGNS AND THEIR PROGRESS." One row per campaign scheduled in this account
// environment, newest first, open, closed and cancelled alike: a closed or a cancelled campaign
// is the proof the check happened, or that it was called off, and stays readable for the
// auditor.
//
// A REVIEWER NEEDS NOTHING HERE. "Each reviewer's slice of a campaign is a task on My tasks &
// attestations … So a reviewer needs no Compliance right of their own beyond their task." This
// list is the whole program, for whoever runs it.
//
// AN OPEN CAMPAIGN'S PROGRESS IS READ FROM ACCOUNT when the list is asked, once for the page:
// "Compliance reads each person's effective access from Account, service to service, the
// Outside Onplo feed included. It never keeps a copy of who has what." How many rows carry a
// decision is not answered yet, because the decisions are the task service's tasks (see the
// top of this file). (This said progress was not answered at all until ONPLO-4588.)
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with GET /access-review-campaigns (the `ListAccessReviewCampaigns` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) ListAccessReviewCampaignsWithResponse(ctx context.Context, params *ListAccessReviewCampaignsParams, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*ListAccessReviewCampaignsResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.ListAccessReviewCampaigns(ctx, params, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseListAccessReviewCampaignsResponse(rsp)
}

// CreateAccessReviewCampaignWithBodyWithResponse Schedule an access-review campaign
//
// "SCHEDULE A RECERTIFICATION — SCOPE, REVIEWERS, CADENCE, DEADLINE; EACH REVIEWER'S DECISION
// LANDS AS THEIR OWN TASK." What is reviewed, who recertifies it, how often it comes round and
// the day it must be done by. It opens Open.
//
// THE SAME ACT ALONE. In a Personal Environment "there is nobody to delegate to … you are the
// reviewer": the one person names themself, and the campaign is the same one. Scheduling one
// is turning the ritual on, which "is OFF by default like every other Compliance feature in a
// personal environment".
//
// A DEADLINE BEFORE TODAY is refused 422 on `deadline` (`deadline_before_today`): a campaign
// is a question asked ahead of its answer. Today is the day in the time zone of the call.
//
// WHAT IT REVIEWS IS THREE CHOICES, WHICH COMBINE (decision 0976): where, who and which
// deploy environments (`AccessReviewScope`). All three are taken. A NAMED SCOPE is one saved
// here, or it is refused 404 `scope_not_found` and nothing is written. (A scope in words was
// refused whole, `scope_not_yet_supported`, until ONPLO-4602; a ticked deploy environment was
// refused, `deploy_environments_not_yet_supported`, until Flows answered whether one exists,
// ONPLO-4659; and a named Scope was refused, `scope_where_not_yet_supported`, until a register
// entry said what it stands for, ONPLO-4699.)
//
// EACH TICKED DEPLOY ENVIRONMENT IS CHECKED IN FLOWS: "a schedule naming a missing one is
// refused, naming it", 404 `deploy_environment_not_found` with every missing id in
// `missing_deploy_environment_ids`. When Flows cannot be asked the answer is
// `flows_unavailable`. Nothing was written in either.
//
// EACH REVIEWER IS A PERSON, CHECKED AGAINST IDENTITY as a control's steward is (decision
// 0670). Anybody who is not a member here today is refused 404 `person_not_found`, and when
// identity cannot be asked the answer is `identity_unavailable`. Nothing was written.
//
// WHAT SCHEDULING DOES NOT DO YET: hand each reviewer their task on My tasks & attestations,
// which is the task service's (decision 0784, point 2). It joins this act the day it does.
// (This said it did not read who has what from Account either, until an open campaign's
// progress did, ONPLO-4588.)
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /access-review-campaigns (the `CreateAccessReviewCampaign` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) CreateAccessReviewCampaignWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*CreateAccessReviewCampaignResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.CreateAccessReviewCampaignWithBody(ctx, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseCreateAccessReviewCampaignResponse(rsp)
}

