// CreateDataRequestWithBodyWithResponse Log a data request
//
// LOGGED THE DAY IT ARRIVED, BECAUSE THE CLOCK RUNS FROM THAT DAY — "a deadline computed from
// the day it arrived, not the day someone noticed". The caller says the day; the deadline is
// one month from it, "the GDPR month", and is answered rather than sent.
//
// A REQUEST IS VALID HOWEVER IT ARRIVES: the trust page's form, an email forwarded in, or typed
// by whoever took the call. "The law does not require a form."
//
// A DAY NO PLACE ON EARTH HAS REACHED YET IS REFUSED, as a field that is wrong
// (`/body/arrived_on`): a request cannot have arrived tomorrow anywhere.
