// ListFindingsWithResponse The findings
//
// WHAT IS WRONG RIGHT NOW — "See what is wrong right now, with severity and fix-by date".
// "A FINDING is something that IS WRONG, today … and it has a deadline rather than a
// probability." One list per account environment, every state in it: a finding that is
// fixed, accepted or a false positive stays on the list and says so.
//
// A ROW IS WHAT IS WRONG, HOW BAD, WHO ANSWERS FOR FIXING IT, WHERE IT SITS, WHAT IT BREAKS,
// WHEN IT MUST BE FIXED BY AND WHERE IT STANDS. Not on it, each with what holds it: how it
// was raised, by hand or by which source, and the evidence of its fix (ONPLO-1969, points 6
// and 1); and its effectiveness re-check, whose "one cycle" has no length (point 4).
//
// NO FILTER YET. The page's saved Nonconformities filter is the findings whose Against names
// a framework requirement. One can be named since ONPLO-4571, and each such finding answers
// it in `against`; a list narrowed to them is not served yet. (This said no requirement could
// be named here until then, ONPLO-1629 point 6.)
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with GET /findings (the `ListFindings` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) ListFindingsWithResponse(ctx context.Context, params *ListFindingsParams, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*ListFindingsResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.ListFindings(ctx, params, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseListFindingsResponse(rsp)
}

// CreateFindingWithBodyWithResponse Add a finding by hand
//
// "ADD A FINDING BY HAND, BESIDE THE ONES SCANNERS AND REVIEWS RAISE." What is wrong, how
// bad, who answers for fixing it and where it sits — the required fields of the screen. It
// starts Open.
//
// THE STEWARD IS SAID, NEVER DEFAULTED, as a control's is. The screen fills in "the steward
// of the thing it sits on", and no register entry here names one yet (ONPLO-1633, point 4),
// so a client sends the person. They are asked of identity exactly as a control's steward is
// (decision 0670): anybody who is not a member here today is refused `steward_not_found`,
// and when identity cannot be asked the answer is `identity_unavailable`. In both nothing
// was written.
//
// WHERE IS "REQUIRED UNLESS AGAINST NAMES A FRAMEWORK REQUIREMENT", AND IT IS A REGISTER
// ENTRY. A finding that names a requirement may sit on nothing; any other finding left without
// `where` is refused 422 (`finding_where_missing`), and nothing is written. "The asset, system
// or vendor it sits on": an entry of the asset and data register is the one of those this
// API has. A vendor is not declared (ONPLO-1635), and no page says a device is an entry of
// the register (ONPLO-1969, point 7). An id that names no entry is refused
// `register_entry_not_found`, and nothing is written. (Where was required here until
// ONPLO-4571, because no requirement could be named.)
//
// AGAINST MAY NAME A CONTROL, A FRAMEWORK REQUIREMENT, OR NOTHING. "The control or FRAMEWORK
// REQUIREMENT this breaks. Pointing it at a requirement is what makes this finding a
// nonconformity; nothing else has to be set." A requirement is one Onplo ships for a
// framework in scope in this account environment, by the id `listFrameworkRequirements`
// answers. An id that names no control in this library is refused `control_not_found`, one
// that names no requirement of a framework in scope here `requirement_not_found`, and nothing
// is written.
//
// FIX BY IS NEVER SENT. It is "computed from severity against the REMEDIATION WINDOWS you
// set once in Settings", and the answer carries it: "It counts from the moment the finding was
// raised: raised on 1 March at High, it is due 31 March" — the day it was raised in the time
// zone of the call that raised it, plus its severity's window. (This said what the days are
// counted from was on no page until ONPLO-1633, point 5, wrote it.)
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /findings (the `CreateFinding` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) CreateFindingWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*CreateFindingResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.CreateFindingWithBody(ctx, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseCreateFindingResponse(rsp)
}

