// ListDutyDocumentsWithResponse A framework's duty documents
//
// THE DOCUMENTS ONE FRAMEWORK OWES, EACH AS IT STANDS: the approved version, and any newer
// draft beside it. The catalogue's row: "See the Statement of Applicability and the system
// description — the approved version and any newer draft beside it."
//
// WHICH DOCUMENTS. Every framework has a Statement of Applicability, a custom one too: "A
// requirement of a custom framework carries the same four", and one of the four is whether it
// is in scope or excluded on it (decision 0783, point 6). The system description is SOC 2's:
// "the SOC 2 system description arrives the same way as an assembled SKELETON". A document
// not yet generated is not in the list.
//
// A NEW DRAFT NEVER TAKES THE APPROVED VERSION'S PLACE. "When the underlying data changes
// the content, a new draft appears beside the approved version, and the approved version
// stays the approved one until somebody approves the new draft" (decision 0783, point 9).
// Both are files in Storage, "under System → Compliance", and each version here names the
// one reading of its file it is.
//
// NOTHING IS GENERATED YET, SO EVERY FRAMEWORK LISTS NONE. Rendering a document into Storage
// waits on Storage holding the file (ONPLO-2922, ONPLO-2921); this read answers what is
// there, and today that is an empty list.
//
// A PERMISSION OF ITS OWN, beside approving: "Seeing the Statement of Applicability and the
// system description is one permission, and approving them is another." A framework removed
// from scope is not one, and answers `not_found`.
