// SendIncidentNoticeWithBodyWithResponse Send a signed-off notice
//
// "SEND AN APPROVED BREACH NOTICE TO THE AFFECTED PEOPLE AND TO CUSTOMERS." The version the
// caller read, signed off, goes to everyone confirmed, one mail each, and the answer is the
// notice, sent. Sending is its own act, beside signing it off.
//
// THE MAIL, as the Incidents page settles it (ONPLO-4974). From the company's name, "via Onplo".
// Its subject is Onplo's own, "A security incident that may affect your data", and its body is
// the notice's parts in the page's order, each under its heading, with nothing added. It goes
// out in the notice's language: its words untranslated, and the subject and headings Onplo's
// own in that language where Onplo has them and in English where it does not yet. It is a
// notification to both audiences, so it carries no unsubscribe link.
//
// EACH MAIL IS HANDED TO DELIVERY, which sends it and reports whether it arrived. Which address
// was delivered or bounced is not on the notice yet: that is heard from Delivery in a later
// change (ONPLO-3923).
//
// SENDING IT FILES THE STEP IT MEETS. "Sending a notice records the step of the obligation that
// names its audience, with the moment": the `notice` step of each obligation to that audience
// that is still running and not filed is recorded as filed at that moment, by the sender, naming
// the notice (`IncidentObligationFiling.sent_notice_id`). A bounce does not undo it. A correction
// sent later files nothing more, because the step is filed already.
//
// A SENT NOTICE IS NEVER CHANGED. Its words, its recipients and its sign-off stay as they were
// sent, and each of those acts is refused on it, `notice_sent`. A correction is a new notice to
// the same audience (`draftIncidentNotice`), and both are kept.
//
// REFUSED, AND WRITES NOTHING. Not signed off is `notice_not_signed_off`. Changed since that
// version is `notice_changed`, so nothing is sent unseen. Sent already is `notice_sent`. A notice
// with no language, one drafted before a notice carried one, is `notice_language_missing`, and
// a change gives it one. A CLOSED INCIDENT IS READ AND NOT WORKED, `incident_closed`.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /incidents/{incident_id}/notices/{notice_id}/sending (the `SendIncidentNotice` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) SendIncidentNoticeWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, incidentId IncidentId, noticeId IncidentNoticeId, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*SendIncidentNoticeResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.SendIncidentNoticeWithBody(ctx, incidentId, noticeId, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseSendIncidentNoticeResponse(rsp)
}

