// PlaceLegalHoldWithBodyWithResponse Place a legal hold
//
// IT FREEZES, AND IT IS IN FORCE WHEN THIS ANSWERS. Everything the hold names, everything
// inside what it names, and everything that arrives there later can no longer be ERASED:
// "automatic deletion stops, retention schedules stop, and what a person deletes for good
// becomes a ghost". A `201` means the service that keeps a held thing from being erased has
// been told and has answered — never that it will be told.
//
// IT REFUSES NO DELETE (decision 0672). A person who deletes a held thing for good is not
// stopped. The thing goes out of use at once and stays behind as a ghost — "a greyed row
// saying Compliance keeps it" — until no hold covers it, and is erased then. (This paragraph
// said "the erase button says why it cannot run" until that ruling.)
//
// `freeze_unavailable` MEANS NO HOLD IS IN FORCE. A legal act must never look done when it is
// not: if the freeze could not be told, nothing was placed, and the call is made again.
//
// EVERY THING AND EVERY PERSON IT NAMES IS ASKED OF IDENTITY FIRST: whether it is in this
// account environment. One that is not answers `held_thing_not_found`; when identity cannot be
// asked the answer is `identity_unavailable`. Either way nothing was placed. Identity is asked
// whether each is THERE, never what it is: a hold still grants nobody access.
//
// IT IS A NAMED PERSON'S ACT, ALWAYS. Ring 1: a raw key is refused whatever its scopes, and
// no agent may place one at any tier. The record carries who placed it and when, computed
// and never typed.
//
// IT TAKES THE MATTER, WHAT IS HELD, THE REASON AND THE AUTHORITY — the four required rows of
// the configuration. The reason and the authority are kept as evidence: this is the record
// an auditor asks for.
//
// A HOLD GRANTS NOBODY ACCESS AND HIDES NOTHING. It does not let its placer open what it
// names, and it never hides content from its owner. It only stops deletion — freezing is not
// seizing. So naming a thing here asks no question about that thing.
//
// EVERY HOLD PLACED HERE IS A VISIBLE ONE: a badge on each held item, and the owners told on
// release. The Confidential mode is another operation with a permission of its own,
// `placeConfidentialHold`, never a flag here: one operation carries exactly one permission.
//
// PLACED WHOLE. There is no adding to a hold afterwards; a second hold may name more.
//
// PEOPLE FIRST (decision 0731, point 4). A hold names people, as Google Vault and Microsoft
// Purview hold custodians, and any shared place its placer can see; "a thing you cannot see
// is held by holding its person".
//
// ONE NARROWING FOR THE WHOLE HOLD (decision 0931). `narrowed_by` says how, and leaving it out
// holds everything named. What the deletion service does with it, and a place the placer
// cannot see, are at the top of this file.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /legal-holds (the `PlaceLegalHold` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) PlaceLegalHoldWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*PlaceLegalHoldResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.PlaceLegalHoldWithBody(ctx, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParsePlaceLegalHoldResponse(rsp)
}

