// GetHoldGhostCountWithResponse How many ghosts a hold alone keeps
//
// THE NUMBER ON THE RELEASE CONFIRM — "The confirm says how many ghosts will go." A ghost is
// what somebody deleted for good while the hold stood (decision 0672), and releasing the hold
// erases the ones it alone keeps. This is that number, asked before the release is pressed.
//
// A NUMBER, AND NOTHING OF WHAT THE THINGS ARE. The permission is "a number, and nothing of
// what the things are", so no name, kind or id of a ghost is answered here or anywhere in
// this API.
//
// ALONE MEANS NO OTHER HOLD IN FORCE KEEPS IT. A ghost another hold also covers stays when this
// one is released, so it is not counted (decision 0686). Neither is what only waits because a
// ghost sits inside it: a folder nobody may see again is not a ghost.
