// AddHoldHiddenFromWithBodyWithResponse Hide a hold from more people
//
// THE LIST CHANGES ONE WAY. "A name can be added, as an act of its own with its reason and
// its audit line. A name is never taken off, because that shows the person a hold that was
// hidden from them; whoever wants that releases the hold." An investigation widens; it is
// never narrowed by quietly telling somebody.
//
// FROM THE MOMENT THIS ANSWERS, the hold is hidden from the people added as from the ones it
// was placed with. What they saw of it before is not undone: a name is best given when the
// hold is placed.
//
// EACH PERSON NAMED IS SOMEBODY IN THIS ACCOUNT ENVIRONMENT, asked of the identity service
// first, as `placeConfidentialHold` asks: `hidden_from_not_found`, or `identity_unavailable`
// with nothing added.
//
// WHOEVER ADDS IS NEVER ON IT, as whoever places it is not: the caller's own name is the 422 at
// `person_ids` (`hidden_from_names_the_adder`), and nothing is asked or added.
//
// ALL OF THEM OR NONE OF THEM. A refused add adds no name. A NAME ALREADY ON THE LIST COSTS
// NOTHING and is not added twice, so the same request sent again adds nobody and answers
// `added_count: 0` — a retry of an add whose answer was lost is not a second add.
//
// THREE THINGS REFUSE IT, each under its own code: the hold was released
// (`legal_hold_already_released`); the hold is a visible one, which is hidden from nobody and
// cannot be made Confidential afterwards (`legal_hold_not_confidential`); and the list would
// pass a hundred people (`hidden_from_list_full`).
//
// IT ANSWERS HOW MANY WERE NEW, AND NOT THE LIST. Seeing the list is `listHoldHiddenFrom`,
// on its own permission; this one adds to it.
//
// A PERSON ON THE LIST IS ANSWERED `not_found`, as for an id that names nothing — whatever
// permission they hold. Nobody adds to a hold that, for them, is not there.
//
// THE HOLD IS JUDGED BEFORE THE PEOPLE. A hold that is not there, is released or is a visible
// one is refused before identity is asked about anybody, so those answers say nothing about
// the names sent.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /legal-holds/{legal_hold_id}/hidden-from (the `AddHoldHiddenFrom` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) AddHoldHiddenFromWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, legalHoldId LegalHoldId, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*AddHoldHiddenFromResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.AddHoldHiddenFromWithBody(ctx, legalHoldId, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseAddHoldHiddenFromResponse(rsp)
}

