// StartPolicyDocumentSaveWithBodyWithResponse Start saving the edit of a policy started from a template
//
// A POLICY STARTED FROM ONE OF ONPLO'S TEMPLATES HAS ITS DOCUMENT IN STORAGE, UNDER SYSTEM →
// COMPLIANCE → POLICIES, and a person cannot save into a file there. So its edit is saved
// through Compliance: "Compliance's door writes the save into the System-zone file" (the
// Policies page). A policy written from your own document is edited in Storage, where that
// document is, and is refused here with `policy_not_from_template`.
//
// THREE STEPS, as an evidence upload takes. This answers a save on its way: its id, and an
// address. Send the whole edited document to the address with one `PUT`, then call
// `completePolicyDocumentSave`. NOTHING IS SAVED UNTIL THAT ANSWERS. Saving it makes no
// version: the next version is made from it with `createPolicyVersion`, as for any policy.
//
// THE ADDRESS IS A CREDENTIAL WHILE IT LIVES. Never put it in a log, a referrer or an
// analytics trail.
//
// "THE EDIT IS MARKDOWN ONLY, AT MOST 1 MB": 1 MB is 1,000,000 bytes, and a larger
// `size_bytes` is refused before an address is issued. Whether it is Markdown is read from the
// bytes when the save completes.
//
// "SAVING THE EDIT OF A POLICY STARTED FROM A TEMPLATE IS WRITING A POLICY TOO, under Manage
// the program, and it needs Policy templates & editor (Premium)", so its permission is
// `updatePolicy`'s. Without your Premium seat in this account environment the answer is 409
// `needs_premium`, "with the feature named", and nothing was asked of Storage. The policy
// still shows. WHEN ACCOUNT CANNOT BE ASKED, the answer is 503 `account_unavailable`, never
// 409 `needs_premium` in its place.
//
// A RETIRED POLICY IS READ AND NOT CHANGED, and is refused with `policy_retired`. NO ROOM LEFT
// IN STORAGE is 409 `quota_full`. Storage that could not be asked is `storage_unavailable`,
// never a no: ask again.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /policies/{policy_id}/document-saves (the `StartPolicyDocumentSave` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) StartPolicyDocumentSaveWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, policyId PolicyId, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*StartPolicyDocumentSaveResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.StartPolicyDocumentSaveWithBody(ctx, policyId, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseStartPolicyDocumentSaveResponse(rsp)
}

