// RetirePolicyWithResponse Retire a policy
//
// "A POLICY IS RETIRED, NEVER DELETED" (decision 0784, point 4). It leaves the library's
// current list, the acknowledgement tasks still open for it close, and its record stays
// readable under Retired: every version, who approved it and who acknowledged it.
//
// A POST AND NOT A DELETE, as retiring a vendor is, because the record does not go. The
// permission is the catalogue's `.delete`: "Retire a policy … Never undone." A policy needed
// again is written as a new one.
//
// RETIRING WHAT IS ALREADY RETIRED CHANGES NOTHING and answers the same policy, with the
// moment it was first retired.
//
// THE OPEN TASKS ARE CLOSED FIRST: each is cancelled on the platform's one task list, and a
// task somebody already finished stays finished. When the task service cannot be reached the
// policy is not retired: 503 `tasks_unavailable`, and the same request can be sent again.
// Retiring again closes any task still open.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /policies/{policy_id}/retire (the `RetirePolicy` operationId).
