// PublishPolicyVersionWithBodyWithResponse Publish an approved version
//
// "PUBLISH AN APPROVED VERSION SO THE RIGHT STAFF ARE ASKED TO ACKNOWLEDGE IT." One version
// is published at a time: publishing version 4 replaces version 3, which stays readable with
// its acknowledgements (decision 0784, point 3). Ring 1, and never an agent: publishing picks
// an audience (decision 0501).
//
// EVERYBODY IS ASKED AGAIN, UNLESS IT IS WORDING ONLY. Everybody the policy is set to be
// acknowledged by gets a new task, "because what they agreed to has changed". Sent with
// `wording_only` and its written reason, nobody is asked again and earlier acknowledgements
// carry over, still naming the version they were given on. The reason is kept on the version.
//
// THE TASK IS ON THE PLATFORM'S ONE TASK LIST (decision 0784, point 2): given to the person,
// made by whoever published. Who is asked is the policy's list, and `listPolicyAcknowledgements`
// reads it.
//
// A TEAM IS ASKED PERSON BY PERSON (decision 0891): each member of each team named, as identity
// answers them now, gets a task of their own, and somebody named and in a team, or in two
// teams, gets one. Identity is asked as the caller, while serving this operation. A team
// deleted since it was named asks nobody, and publishing goes on. Somebody who joins a team
// afterwards is asked by the next version published, as somebody added to the list is. A task still open for the version this one replaces is cancelled, because that
// version can no longer be acknowledged; wording only cancels nothing, and acknowledging the
// version published now finishes the task still open. When the task service cannot be reached
// nothing is published: 503 `tasks_unavailable`, and the same request can be sent again.
//
// ONLY AN APPROVED VERSION NEWER THAN THE ONE PUBLISHED IS PUBLISHED. A draft is refused with
// `version_not_approved`; a version no newer than the published one with
// `version_not_newer`; any version of a retired policy with `policy_retired`.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /policies/{policy_id}/versions/{version_number}/publish (the `PublishPolicyVersion` operationId).
