// ApproveManagementReviewWithResponse Approve a management review
//
// "APPROVE A MANAGEMENT REVIEW — IT FREEZES AND DATES THE PACK." The caller's approval of one
// review, in their own name: who approved it is written from the call's credential, never
// from the request. Ring 1, and never an agent: "approving is signing on somebody's behalf,
// and four-eyes means the eyes are human".
//
// ONE APPROVAL MAKES A REVIEW APPROVED, UNTIL THE COMPANY'S SIGN-OFF SETTING SAYS MORE. "Who
// may approve, how many approvals it needs and whether a note is required follow the
// company's sign-off setting (decision 0731), as accepting a risk does." That setting's page
// and defaults are not written (ONPLO-1864); it is not declared here, and joins this act the
// day it is. So whether an attendee, or somebody whose controls the review judged, may
// approve is not ruled either, and is not refused. "In a Personal Environment the one person
// approves."
//
// APPROVING DATES THE REVIEW, NEVER UNDONE: "what management knew, and when, needs a dated
// answer". `approved_at` is that date. The pack it freezes and the tasks its decisions become
// are not declared yet (see the top of this file), and join this act the day they are.
//
// ONLY A MANAGEMENT REVIEW NOT YET APPROVED IS APPROVED. An internal audit round is refused
// `not_a_management_review`, and a review already approved `review_already_approved`; in
// both, nothing changes.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
