// RecordProgramReviewVerdictWithBodyWithResponse Record the verdict on one control a round tests
//
// "Each tested item gets a verdict — conforms · does not conform · an observation — with the
// sample recorded." One control of the round, judged once: the verdict is written in the
// caller's own name, from the call's credential, and is never changed or taken back, because
// it is the evidence the round leaves.
//
// EVERY DOES NOT CONFORM OPENS A FINDING, in the same transaction. "It is raised against the
// tested control": its Against is that control. "The person who records 'does not conform'
// chooses its severity, and there is no default, because a guessed severity sets a false
// fix-by date": `severity` is required with it, and refused with any other verdict. "Its
// steward is the steward of that control": copied from the control as it stands, never sent.
// "It sits on the control's own register entry when the control has one, and otherwise the
// same person picks the entry": no control here names a register entry yet, so the caller
// picks it every time, and `register_entry_id` is required. What is wrong, in the person's
// words, is `note`, which is required with it and becomes the finding's `what_is_wrong`. Its
// fix-by date is counted from its severity exactly as `createFinding` counts one. The verdict
// answers the finding's id.
//
// THE LAST VERDICT COMPLETES THE ROUND. When every control the round tests has one, the round's
// `completed_at` is set, and the next round's due date counts from it (`getProgramReviewDueDates`).
//
// IN EVERY REFUSAL HERE NOTHING WAS WRITTEN: a management review (`not_an_internal_audit_round`),
// a control the round does not test (`control_not_in_round`), a control already judged in it
// (`verdict_already_recorded`), and a register entry that is not in this register
// (`register_entry_not_found`).
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /program-reviews/{program_review_id}/verdicts (the `RecordProgramReviewVerdict` operationId).
