// GetRiskScaleWithResponse Read the scale the risk register scores on
//
// "SEE THE SCALE THE RISK REGISTER SCORES ON." One setting per account environment: "3×3
// default · 5×5 · custom level labels". The answer is how many levels each axis has, which
// is the highest pick `createRisk` and `updateRisk` take, and what each level of each axis is
// called. An account environment that never chose answers 3, with no level named.
//
// SEEING IT IS A PERMISSION OF ITS OWN, beside setting it, "so anybody who scores a risk
// can read what each level means". The catalogue gained it with decision 0804, point 3.
// Every look is recorded (decision 0675).
//
// (This said the answer "carries the count alone", that no page says whether a label is per
// axis, and that nothing can change the scale yet, so every account environment answers 3,
// until the Risk scoring page answered ONPLO-1633, point 8, and `setRiskScale` was declared.)
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with GET /risk-scale (the `GetRiskScale` operationId).
