//
// A SCOPE FILTERS, IT NEVER FORKS. "No second control library, no second risk register, no
// separate evidence store, and no per-scope control status." So this makes a selection and
// nothing else: no control, risk or piece of evidence is copied, moved or marked by it.
//
// ITS SYSTEMS ARE ENTRIES OF THIS REGISTER — "a scope is a saved selection of it, not a
// second register". An id that names no entry here is refused `register_entry_not_found`,
// and nothing is written. One entry may be in several scopes.
//
// THE TEAMS THAT OPERATE IT ARE TEAMS OF THIS ACCOUNT ENVIRONMENT — "Who operates it (read
// from Account)", default none. Identity is asked about every one named, as the caller and
// while serving this operation, before anything is written (ONPLO-3314). One that is not a
// team here — no such id, another environment's, or a team deleted — is refused
// `team_not_found`, and nothing is written; the answer never says which. When identity cannot
// be asked the answer is `identity_unavailable` and nothing is written: a team nobody could
// check is never written down. Naming none asks identity nothing.
//
// A BUSINESS ACCOUNT ENVIRONMENT'S ACT. The catalogue gives this permission to a business
// account environment alone: "personally there is always exactly one" scope, and no field.
//
// NOT HERE, each with what holds it:
//   - SEEING, CHANGING AND REMOVING A SCOPE. No permission exists for any of the three
//     (ONPLO-1635, point 4), so this answer is the only place a scope is read.
//   - A NAME ALREADY IN USE. No page says whether two scopes may carry one name (the same
//     point), so nothing here refuses a name.
//
